  "discussion": {
    "headline": "unseasonably warm through friday with a big cooldown to follow",
    "dateLine": "11:30 a.m. Wednesday, October 14, 2026",
    "excerpt": "Following the 2-4\" soaking from Hurricane Isaias's remnants on Sunday, the second full week of October kicked off on a mostly cloudy, dry and milder note with high temperatures in the low 70s on Monday. Skies then cleared Monday night, and south-southwesterly winds on the backside of a high pressure system ushered unseasonably warm and humid air into the Lower Susquehanna Valley on Tuesday. …",
